{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418173","formula":"C₇H₁₁NO₂","hill":"C7H11NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":7.0,"H":11.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"(2S,4R)-hypoglycin A","ru":"Гипоглицин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hypoglycin A is a naturally occurring amino acid derivative found in the unripened fruit of the ackee tree (Blighia sapida) and in the seeds of the box elder tree (Acer negundo). It is toxic if ingested, and is the causative agent of Jamaican vomiting sickness. A 2017 Lancet report established a link between the consumption of unripened lychees (which contain hypoglycin A or the related chemical compound methylenecyclopropylglycine (MCPG)) resulting in hypoglycaemia and death from acute toxic encephalopathy.","ru":"Гипоглицин (также Гипоглицин А) — органическое соединение, фитотоксин, непротеиногенная аминокислота, производная L-аланина, является высокотоксичным веществом. Контаминант."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":11768666,"mass":141.17,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=C1C[C@@H]1C[C@@H](C(=O)O)N","inchikey":"OOJZCXFXPZGUBJ-RITPCOANSA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-amino-3-[(1R)-2-methylidenecyclopropyl]propanoic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11768666","atoms":21,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.374,"y":1.676,"z":0.147,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.21,"y":-0.278,"z":-0.662,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.158,"y":-1.71,"z":0.317,"el":"N"},{"x":1.438,"y":-0.267,"z":0.444,"el":"C"},{"x":2.349,"y":-1.125,"z":-0.478,"el":"C"},{"x":2.667,"y":0.179,"z":-0.051,"el":"C"},{"x":0.17,"y":0.303,"z":-0.121,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.087,"y":-0.266,"z":0.545,"el":"C"},{"x":3.548,"y":1.155,"z":-0.086,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.342,"y":0.334,"z":-0.055,"el":"C"},{"x":1.402,"y":-0.477,"z":1.504,"el":"H"},{"x":2.077,"y":-1.249,"z":-1.516,"el":"H"},{"x":2.898,"y":-1.94,"z":-0.028,"el":"H"},{"x":0.119